<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="TAM 251" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2008" href="schedule/2008.xml">2008</calendarYear><term id="120088" href="schedule/2008/fall.xml">Fall 2008</term><subject id="TAM" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM.xml">Theoretical and Applied Mechanics</subject></parents><label>Introductory Solid Mechanics</label><description>Relationship between internal stresses and deformations produced by external forces acting on deformable bodies, and design principles based on mechanics of solids: normal stresses, shear stresses, and deformations produced by tensile, compressive, torsional, and bending loading of members; beam deflections; elastic energy and impact; multi-dimensional stress states; buckling of columns. Prerequisite: TAM 210 or TAM 211.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="33482" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/33482.xml">AD1</section><section id="33532" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/33532.xml">AD2</section><section id="34913" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/34913.xml">AD3</section><section id="33294" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/33294.xml">AD4</section><section id="33381" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/33381.xml">AD5</section><section id="34924" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/34924.xml">AD6</section><section id="52451" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/52451.xml">AD7</section><section id="35306" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/35306.xml">AL1</section><section id="35217" href="schedule/2008/fall/TAM/251/35217.xml">AL2</section></sections></ns2:course>